            0.155,
            0.408,
            0.173
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "5 Clausal form"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.186,
            0.568,
            0.201
          ],
          "content": "(6) Convert each sentence below to clausal form."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.211,
            0.403,
            0.227
          ],
          "content": "a. $\\forall y . \\exists x . r ( x , y ) \\lor s ( x , y )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.236,
            0.406,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": "b. $\\forall y . ( \\exists x . r ( x , y ) ) \\rightarrow p ( y )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.261,
            0.407,
            0.277
          ],
          "content": "c. $\\forall y . \\exists x . ( r ( x , y ) \\rightarrow p ( x ) )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.3,
            0.512,
            0.32
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "6 Operator descriptions"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.33,
            0.782,
            0.361
          ],
          "content": "(6) Consider a world with a push-button light switch. Pushing the button changes the state of the light from on to off, or from off to on."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.371,
            0.553,
            0.386
          ],
          "content": "a. Describe this domain in situation calculus."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.213,
            0.396,
            0.662,
            0.412
          ],
          "content": "b. Describe this domain using one or more strips operators."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.434,
            0.387,
            0.454
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "7 GraphPlan"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.465,
            0.784,
            0.511
          ],
          "content": "(13) Draw the graphplan graph for a depth-two plan given the following operator descriptions. Starting state is: not have-keys, not open, not painted. Goal state is: open, painted. Show all mutexes."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.239,
            0.52,
            0.509,
            0.536
          ],
          "content": "• Get Keys: (Pre: ) (Eff: have-keys)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.239,
            0.545,
            0.549,
            0.562
          ],
          "content": "• Open Door: (Pre: not open) (Eff: open)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.239,
            0.571,
            0.567,
            0.587
          ],
          "content": "• Paint Door: (Pre: not open) (Eff: painted)"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.609,
            0.532,
            0.628
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "8 Conditional Probability"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.64,
            0.781,
            0.686
          ],
          "content": "(8) We would like to compute $\\operatorname* { P r } ( a , b | c , d )$ but we only have available to us the following quantities: $\\operatorname* { P r } ( a ) ,   \\operatorname* { P r } ( b ) ,   \\operatorname* { P r } ( c ) ,   \\operatorname* { P r } ( a | d ) ,   \\operatorname* { P r } ( b | d ) ,   \\operatorname* { P r } ( c | d ) ,   \\operatorname* { P r } ( d | a )$ , $\\operatorname* { P r } ( a , b ) ,   \\operatorname* { P r } ( c , d ) ,   \\operatorname* { P r } ( a | c , d ) ,   \\operatorname* { P r } ( b | c , d ) ,   \\operatorname* { P r } ( c | a , b ) ,   \\operatorname* { P r } ( d | a , b )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.686,
            0.783,
            0.732
          ],
          "content": "For each of the assumptions below, give a set of terms that is sufficient to compute the desired probability, or “none” if it can’t be determined from the given quantities."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.741,
            0.636,
            0.756
          ],
          "content": "a. A and B are conditionally independent given C and D"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.765,
            0.635,
            0.781
          ],
          "content": "b. C and D are conditionally independent given A and B"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.791,
            0.431,
            0.806
          ],
          "content": "c. A and B are independent"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.816,
            0.636,
            0.831
          ],
          "content": "d. A, B, and C are all conditionally independent given D"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.494,
            0.877,
